# Global Filter Scrollability & Consistency Update

## Goal Description
Ensure all filter dropdowns across the entire application are scrollable, visually consistent, and use the premium custom dropdown styling. This involves converting remaining native HTML `<select>` elements to custom `<div>` based structures that utilize the `.dropdown-options` class (which has been updated with scrolling capability).

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> This change replaces native browser selects with custom DOM elements. While this provides better styling control and consistency, it requires careful handling of events.
> **Strategy**: We will replace `<select id="X">` with a wrapper `div` and a `<input type="hidden" id="X">`. This allows existing code that reads `.value` to access the selected value without modification. However, we must ensure we programmatically dispatch [change](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/dashboard.js#345-346) events when a custom option is selected so that attached event listeners still fire.

